<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Renaissance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Renaissance was a period of cultural revival in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> from the fourteenth to the sixteenth century, beginning in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and centred on the recovery of classical learning. It drew on Greek texts and scholars from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>, on Arabic science from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> and on the legacy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>. The term is also applied to earlier revivals such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/renaissance.jpg" alt="Renaissance" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sandro Botticelli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sandro_Botticelli_046.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
